[NOTED, not a finding] the cached clean answer does NOT survive the condition clearing
    after the permission was restored: resolve_quarantine -> (KineticsQuarantine, True). The review said the clean answer is 'cached for the rest of the run'; measured, it is not. Restoring the permission moves the signature from (True, None, 'absent') to (True, <identity>, 'regular'), which misses the cache and forces a re-read. The entry is still wrong while the error lasts, and is still removed here on the principle that an answer produced by a failure is not a property of the key -- but the permanence in the review does not reproduce.

